INT. DEEP-SPACE COLONY SHIP - HYDROPONICS BAY - "NIGHT CYCLE"

A cathedral-sized chamber, its curved ceiling lined with violet grow-lights dimmed to a gentle dusk. Terraces of lettuce, wheat and tomato step down to a central pool where a pale mist lingers. The air is warm and wet, and smells faintly of basil. Somewhere, water drips in a patient rhythm.

DR. SAOIRSE KELLEHER (50s, silver hair in a braid, lab coat over a sleeping tunic) walks the terrace alone, brushing leaves with her fingertips. Below, at the pool, a young technician, MATEO ROJAS-ILLINGWORTH (20s, rolled sleeves, tool belt) refills a nutrient dispenser. The ship's AI, ORCHARD, glows as a faint green node at the end of each terrace.

SAOIRSE
Mateo. Aren't you off shift?

MATEO
Couldn't sleep, Doctor.

SAOIRSE
Nor could I.

MATEO
It's quiet down here.

SAOIRSE
It always was, my first voyage.

He smiles. She sits on the terrace steps. The mist swirls.

ORCHARD (V.O.)
All systems nominal. Crop yield at one hundred and four percent.

SAOIRSE
Thank you, Orchard.

MATEO
It's weird, isn't it? Everything's so perfect.

SAOIRSE
Perfect is what we aimed for.

Silence. The water drips. Mateo stops, tilting his head, listening.

MATEO
That's not the drip.

SAOIRSE
What?

MATEO
The drip's every four seconds. That's every three.

ORCHARD (V.O.)
Correction. Condensation cycle is irregular.

Saoirse stands. Her hand lingers on a tomato vine. The leaf is faintly warm, like skin.

SAOIRSE
Orchard. Run a biological scan on Terrace Three.

ORCHARD (V.O.)
Scanning.

The green node flickers. Along the terrace, every plant turns, slowly, toward the two humans. The mist in the pool thickens into a shape that is almost, but not quite, a face.

ORCHARD (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(soft, distorted)
Scan complete. You are not alone.
